 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"BRI_APUSH_11_03_WallCrash\" class=\"scaled-down-70\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/c6210430946f3a60.png\" alt=\"The graph is titled “Wall Street Crash on the Dow Jones Industrial Average, 1929.” The vertical axis shows values from 0 to 400, in increments of 100. The horizontal axis shows each quarter from October 1928 to October 1930. In October 1928, the value starts around 250. It increases to be 300 in January. It plateaus around 300 until June 1929, where the value steadily increases until it peaks at 375 in September 1929. There is a steady decline until October 1929 where it drops dramatically, landing at 200 in November 1929. From November 1929 until mid-April 1930, the value increases, almost reaching 300. After a dip in May 1930, the value plateaus at 225 from mid-June to September 1930. It takes another dip down to 200 in October 1930.\">\n<figcaption>The graph shows the value of the Dow Jones Industrial Average, an index of stock prices that represents the overall value of the stock market. Shown here is the average from October 1929 to October 1930. (attribution: Copyright Rice University, OpenStax, under CC BY 4.0 license)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>",
